WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.880
Welcome to DBL Group's TalentHub!

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.400
A new employee's medical clearance
has two roles: the Medical Officer

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.560
and the Central Medical Officer.
In this video we'll see how the

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.679
Medical Officer submits the examination
report, how the CMO confirms it,

5
00:00:16.799 --> 00:00:21.920
and why nobody is cleared until the
CMO approves. Let's get started!

6
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.030
Both roles are group-wide,
for every unit, granted on Access Control.

7
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.150
In the menu each role has its own page:

8
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:36.150
Medical Clearance for the Medical Officer,
Medical Approvals for the CMO.

9
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.950
Requisitions and Organogram are not
your work, so they are not there.

10
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.350
Sign in with your DBL email and password.
The two roles are kept apart on purpose:

11
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:48.260
holding the CMO role does not
let you write the examination;

12
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.940
one person doing both loses
the second pair of eyes.

13
00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:56.210
How does a candidate reach you?
The recruiter requests a medical test;

14
00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:01.081
Head of Talent Acquisition sets the date,
time and venue and sends.

15
00:01:01.201 --> 00:01:06.131
The medical team gets a letter,
the candidate an appointment.

16
00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:08.970
From then on the candidate
is in your queue.

17
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.120
What the letter holds:
the candidate's list of tests,

18
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:18.960
the one for below forty or for forty
and above, as the recruiter chose,

19
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.480
the reference number,
date, time and venue.

20
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.880
When the candidate arrives,
match them by this reference number.

21
00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:29.230
The Medical Officer's page,
Medical Clearance.

22
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:33.470
At the top, Awaiting exam,
Sent back, and Longest wait.

23
00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:37.590
Each row: the candidate, post,
unit, and how long they have waited.

24
00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:43.340
Open the candidate. The Medical
Fitness Report form, DBL's paper form.

25
00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:48.980
Report details, then the vitals:
height, weight, blood pressure, pulse.

26
00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:54.997
Then vision, including colour vision.
Hearing and speech, with the extremities.

27
00:01:55.117 --> 00:02:00.323
Clinical findings:
past illness and family history.

28
00:02:00.443 --> 00:02:03.690
Blood group. And remarks.

29
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.084
Every section complete, and you can clear.

30
00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.874
Halfway through, Save draft.

31
00:02:10.314 --> 00:02:14.354
If you have the signed report scanned,
Attach signed report;

32
00:02:14.474 --> 00:02:15.594
it is optional.

33
00:02:15.944 --> 00:02:19.344
Finally Fit to Join: Fit or Not fit.

34
00:02:19.784 --> 00:02:25.984
Then Clear candidate, and Confirm
clearance. The form goes to the CMO.

35
00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:29.944
The candidate is not cleared yet;
they are once the CMO confirms.

36
00:02:30.294 --> 00:02:34.494
And if they are not fit?
Set Fit to Join to Not fit,

37
00:02:34.614 --> 00:02:39.374
and instead of Clear candidate use Reject,
then Confirm rejection.

38
00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:43.784
The form goes to the CMO just the same,
as proposed unfit; once confirmed,

39
00:02:43.904 --> 00:02:50.414
the recruiting side is told
and HR decides whether the hire proceeds.

40
00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.254
You only record what you found.

41
00:02:53.604 --> 00:02:58.844
Two extras. Checked by hand records
the result without the form,

42
00:02:58.964 --> 00:03:04.404
with a note, and the record says manual.
And Print, for the file.

43
00:03:04.754 --> 00:03:09.354
If the CMO sends one back,
the row is marked Sent back,

44
00:03:10.194 --> 00:03:14.834
with their note. Re-examine, fix what
was asked, and Clear candidate again.

45
00:03:15.184 --> 00:03:20.664
Now the CMO. Medical Approvals lists
every form the Medical Officers sent:

46
00:03:20.784 --> 00:03:24.287
Awaiting, Proposed fit, Proposed unfit.

47
00:03:24.407 --> 00:03:28.224
Filter, search,
and View findings opens the whole form.

48
00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:33.734
All fine? The tick, Approve.
Several at once, tick their boxes and

49
00:03:33.854 --> 00:03:40.254
Approve with the count. Now the candidate
is cleared and the recruiter is told.

50
00:03:40.604 --> 00:03:44.724
A long list, filter: Unfit first,

51
00:03:44.844 --> 00:03:49.164
those need the closest look.
Search by name or post.

52
00:03:49.514 --> 00:03:54.994
Disagree with a clearance?
The cross, Overturn:

53
00:03:55.354 --> 00:03:58.794
the candidate is not cleared,
and the reason is required.

54
00:03:58.914 --> 00:04:02.954
To change a finding the other way,
Send back. Shown, Cancel.

55
00:04:03.304 --> 00:04:06.864
Something unclear? Send back, with a note.

56
00:04:07.624 --> 00:04:10.944
It returns to the Medical Officer,
marked Sent back.

57
00:04:11.624 --> 00:04:16.984
Once they fix and resend,
Approve. Now, Medical cleared.

58
00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:21.454
After approval the recruiter's
onboarding shows Medical cleared,

59
00:04:21.574 --> 00:04:26.614
and the decision cannot be undone.
So in doubt, Send back first.

60
00:04:26.964 --> 00:04:32.964
Notifications. Medical Officer:
a new candidate in the queue,

61
00:04:33.084 --> 00:04:35.654
the CMO sent one back.

62
00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:39.674
CMO: a new form arrived. By email too,
with Email notifications on in Settings.

63
00:04:39.794 --> 00:04:43.274
Under the Notifications tab in Settings,
Email notifications;

64
00:04:43.394 --> 00:04:45.874
turn it off if you like,
the bell still rings.

65
00:04:46.224 --> 00:04:49.544
Questions. The appointment is booked,
why not in my queue?

66
00:04:49.824 --> 00:04:54.184
HR's documents or facilities step
is not done; they appear once it is.

67
00:04:55.023 --> 00:04:58.304
Clear without every section?
Checked by hand.

68
00:04:58.424 --> 00:05:04.539
Can the CMO edit my form? No: confirm,
overturn or send back, those three only.

69
00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:07.329
Want to attach the report after clearing?

70
00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:11.329
Not any more; ask the CMO to Send back.

71
00:05:11.449 --> 00:05:15.369
Print Medical Fitness Report
works at any time, for the file.

72
00:05:15.719 --> 00:05:21.199
In short. Medical Officer:
Medical Clearance,

73
00:05:21.319 --> 00:05:24.159
the form, Fit to Join, Clear candidate.

74
00:05:24.519 --> 00:05:30.879
CMO: Medical Approvals,
Approve, Overturn, or Send back.

75
00:05:31.718 --> 00:05:36.039
The full guide is a PDF under Tutorials.
Thank you.

